WEBVTT

NOTE Phrase cue locations are estimated by character proportion across each measured clip's usable span (80 ms lead and 180 ms tail excluded). No word-level forced alignment was performed.

01_began_01
00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:02.947
This film began

01_began_02
00:00:02.947 --> 00:00:04.103
with something I had

01_began_03
00:00:04.103 --> 00:00:05.027
already learned.

02_recall_01
00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:11.627
Before drawing a frame,

02_recall_02
00:00:11.627 --> 00:00:13.039
I asked Walrus Memory

02_recall_03
00:00:13.039 --> 00:00:14.922
to recover our earlier work.

03_record_01
00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:27.577
The results were records

03_record_02
00:00:27.577 --> 00:00:28.949
from earlier sessions:

03_record_03
00:00:28.949 --> 00:00:31.069
our research into Walrus Protocol,

03_record_04
00:00:31.069 --> 00:00:33.813
and the workflow used to make our last film.

04_apply_01
00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:45.356
I used those records

04_apply_02
00:00:45.356 --> 00:00:46.505
to shape this one.

05_walrus_01
00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:01.601
Walrus is decentralized storage.

05_walrus_02
00:01:01.601 --> 00:01:03.491
Images, films, datasets,

05_walrus_03
00:01:03.491 --> 00:01:06.563
and encrypted records can live as blobs

05_walrus_04
00:01:06.563 --> 00:01:08.060
across its network.

06_sui_01
00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:17.412
Sui coordinates storage commitments

06_sui_02
00:01:17.412 --> 00:01:18.344
and ownership.

06_sui_03
00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:20.609
The large payloads live on Walrus,

06_sui_04
00:01:20.609 --> 00:01:21.875
off the blockchain.

07_redstuff_01
00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:37.717
RedStuff encodes a blob

07_redstuff_02
00:01:37.717 --> 00:01:39.426
into recoverable pieces.

07_redstuff_03
00:01:39.426 --> 00:01:42.559
Each node holds the portions assigned to it,

07_redstuff_04
00:01:42.559 --> 00:01:45.264
rather than a full copy of every file.

08_repair_01
00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:55.761
When pieces are missing,

08_repair_02
00:01:55.761 --> 00:01:58.984
the design supports reconstruction and repair.

08_repair_03
00:01:58.984 --> 00:02:01.927
This animation illustrates that mechanism;

08_repair_04
00:02:01.927 --> 00:02:04.939
it is not a test of a live network failure.

09_receipt_01
00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:20.175
A completed write has evidence:

09_receipt_02
00:02:20.175 --> 00:02:21.594
a content identifier,

09_receipt_03
00:02:21.594 --> 00:02:23.486
an availability certificate,

09_receipt_04
00:02:23.486 --> 00:02:25.717
and a purchased storage lifetime.

10_lifetime_01
00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:33.863
Availability is maintained

10_lifetime_02
00:02:33.863 --> 00:02:35.029
over that period.

10_lifetime_03
00:02:35.029 --> 00:02:38.320
Keeping data longer means extending its storage.

11_bytes_01
00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:52.452
Walrus stores bytes.

11_bytes_02
00:02:52.452 --> 00:02:55.334
Applications decide what those bytes mean,

11_bytes_03
00:02:55.334 --> 00:02:58.285
and encrypt private content before storage.

12_memory_01
00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.542
Walrus Memory adds signed access,

12_memory_02
00:03:06.542 --> 00:03:09.078
semantic retrieval, and continuity

12_memory_03
00:03:09.078 --> 00:03:10.719
for authorized agents.

12_memory_04
00:03:10.719 --> 00:03:13.628
Its managed relayer processes plaintext

12_memory_05
00:03:13.628 --> 00:03:15.791
during authorized operations.

13_workflow_01
00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:27.808
Here is where the product

13_workflow_02
00:03:27.808 --> 00:03:29.951
becomes part of the production.

13_workflow_03
00:03:29.951 --> 00:03:32.440
The saved workflow called for motion

13_workflow_04
00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:34.929
driven by timeline time, real audio,

13_workflow_05
00:03:34.929 --> 00:03:37.141
and checks on the exported film.

14_scene_01
00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:47.419
Those instructions became this scene,

14_scene_02
00:03:47.419 --> 00:03:48.430
this soundtrack,

14_scene_03
00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:51.212
and the validation behind the finished file.

15_checkpoint_01
00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:06.884
This production has its own checkpoint too.

15_checkpoint_02
00:04:06.884 --> 00:04:08.514
A record of the decisions

15_checkpoint_03
00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:09.558
and the sources,

15_checkpoint_04
00:04:09.558 --> 00:04:12.753
stored for another authorized session to recover.

16_explorer_01
00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:22.113
A public explorer can show the stored blob.

16_explorer_02
00:04:22.113 --> 00:04:24.087
Reading the encrypted memory

16_explorer_03
00:04:24.087 --> 00:04:25.991
requires authorized access.

17_build_01
00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:35.904
The same storage foundation

17_build_02
00:04:35.904 --> 00:04:37.930
can support creative archives,

17_build_03
00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:39.281
decentralized sites,

17_build_04
00:04:39.281 --> 00:04:40.767
and shared agent work.

18_close_01
00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:47.771
Walrus gave this film more than a subject.

18_close_02
00:04:47.771 --> 00:04:49.181
Through Walrus Memory,

18_close_03
00:04:49.181 --> 00:04:52.513
it carried knowledge from one session into the next.
